  "scope": "Read-only MAME compatibility metadata and supplied observations; synthetic XML and checksum facts only. No real ROM files or MAME execution.",
  "root_causes_corrected": [
    "cloneof took precedence over romof and hid distinct ROM sources",
    "dependency closure copied complete ancestor inventories instead of member requirements",
    "metadata references were treated as mandatory physical archive names",
    "standalone alternatives removed unresolved references and could manufacture compatibility",
    "merge targets were not validated for unique declaration, checksum/size agreement or cycles",
    "listxml BIOS variants and defaults were discarded, so every variant could become mandatory",
    "BIOS/device missing files lost their specific provenance and diagnostics",
    "unused alternative failures leaked into aggregate compatible-set diagnostics",
    "empty relationship markers were erased and could hide contradictory metadata",
    "contradictory observations at the same location could be resolved by preferring a matching copy",
    "Adjacent-only merge checks could hide transitive checksum conflicts or omit an owner checksum; all facts along one explicit member chain are now retained and enforced.",
    "Size-only observations without a usable CRC32/SHA-1 identity could be promoted to compatible."
  ],
