  "schema_compatibility": {
    "old_version": 1,
    "new_version": 2,
    "changes": "Add dependency resolution/provenance, effective BIOS selections, layout and verified observed-ROM records. Existing function signatures and expected/observed ROM shapes remain; new layout/BIOS methods are additive. Explicit borrowed-member declaration chains retain original per-set checksums; resolved requirements enforce their accumulated constraints without adding the provider inventory.",
    "rust_struct_literals": "MameDependencyEvidence now requires resolution; MameSetCompatibility now includes verified_roms. The existing internal literal is updated.",
    "cached_metadata": "Reparse older listxml artifacts to recover BIOS declarations/defaults and retained empty markers; cached data that discarded those facts cannot recreate them."
  },
  "remaining_limitations": [
    "Explicit merged disk requirements are conservatively Unknown; CHD parent chains, recovery and reconstruction are outside this change.",
    "No general software-list, sample, image-loader or live slot-configuration evaluation is added.",
    "BIOS variants require an unambiguous declared default, a single variant or explicit caller selection. Invalid/ambiguous choices remain Unknown.",
    "Duplicate referenced declarations, unsupported structures/load flags and chains deeper than the existing 64-node bound remain Unknown.",
    "The evaluator consumes gathered configured-rompath evidence; it performs no filesystem scan, hashing, MAME invocation or live launch/configuration validation. Ordering of copies across rompaths is not represented.",
    "Only available CRC32/SHA-1 and size facts can prove ROM identity in the current observed-ROM interface; unproven identity remains Unknown."
  ],
